[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3684626514","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114228#issuecomment-3684626514","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114228","id":3684626514,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7bnvBS","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-23T00:22:57Z","updated_at":"2025-12-23T00:38:59Z","body":"<img width=\"798\" height=\"113\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/49a493c2-1454-4e0c-a86f-5b06c29d61ee\" />\n\nWhen configuring the Input Map, you can select the device number.\n\nUnfortunately, device `0` is currently being used by multiple types of devices.\n\n- Godot does not distinguish between keyboard and mouse devices. The device ID for all keyboard and mouse events is `0`. Therefore, even if you have multiple sets of keyboards and mice, it's still difficult to distinguish between them.\n- The joypad devices are also numbered starting from `0`.\n\nIdeally, a keyboard and mouse combination should be equivalent to a gamepad. They should be numbered sequentially together. At that time, it might be necessary to provide preset configurations for dynamic device binding.\n\n\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3684626514/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765261277","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114228#issuecomment-3765261277","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114228","id":3765261277,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gbVPd","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T12:54:20Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T13:00:12Z","body":"Hello, I can't reproduce the issue (Godot 4.5) until I move a stick on my controller, after that I get a vector with a very small X value and almost 1 Y value.\nI don't think that's a bug, that's just how `get_vector()` works, it gets the *raw* strength of all 4 actions (before actions' deadzone comes in), combines them into a vector, and applies deadzone *after* it constructs the vector and applies it to the vector length, not the individual axes. And if the vector's length is above 1, it modifies it to be of length 1.\nSince the joysticks aren't perfect, they still return some values even at rest, which is what's happening here. Since the vector's horizontal value isn't 0, the vertical value won't be exactly 1.\n\nThis probably needs to be documented.\n\nAlthough the current behaviour can be changed, I will think about a solution.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3765261277/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3766434315","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/114228#issuecomment-3766434315","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/114228","id":3766434315,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7gfzoL","user":{"login":"matjlars","id":74511919,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc0NTExOTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/74511919?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/matjlars","html_url":"https://github.com/matjlars","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matjlars/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matjlars/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matjlars/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matjlars/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matjlars/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matjlars/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matjlars/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matjlars/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/matjlars/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-19T05:11:57Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T05:11:57Z","body":"In my opinion, it makes the most sense to use the deadzone on each input device and then add them together. The purpose of the deadzone is to not get little drifty values, but the little drifty values shine through currently in my described scenario. For example consider the scenario in which eight gamepads are plugged in. It would make sense to apply the deadzone to all eight, rather than get a huge drift after they're all summed up.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3766434315/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]